{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775348535-6vQsM9T97vVIywIisOrg","role":"assistant","created":1775348545,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the table structure, I now see what's happening!\n\nThe table has data arranged in columns like this:\n- Row 1 (actual row 1 of data): 1936-Jan with partially tax-exempt and taxable -> 1941-Jan with partially tax-exempt and taxable -> 1944-Jan with partially tax-exempt, taxable, AND corporate\n\nSo each row has THREE sets of columns:\n- First set: Year from 1936 (Jan-Jun and the full year)\n- Second set: Year from 1941  \n- Third set: Year from 1944-1946\n\nThe CORPORATE bond data only appears starting from the 1944 column!\n\nSo the data format is:\n- 1936 column group: partially tax-exempt Treasury, taxable Treasury\n- 1941 column group: partially tax-exempt Treasury, taxable Treasury  \n- 1944+ column group: partially tax-exempt Treasury, taxable Treasury, high-grade corporate\n\nLooking at rows 2-7 of the data (Feb through July of 1936 and corresponding months of 1941 and 1944), I can see:\n- Feb 1936: 2.68, 3.15 | Feb 1941: 2.22, 2.71 | Feb 1944: 1.93, 2.49, 2.65\n- Mar 1936: 2.67, 3.16 | Mar 1941: 2.12, 2.73 | Mar 1944: 1.91, 2.48, 2.64\n- Apr 1936: 2.66, 3.25 | Apr 1941: 2.07, 2.76 | Apr 1944: 1.94, 2.48, 2.61\n- May 1936: 2.56, 3.14 | May 1941: 2.04, 2.75 | May 1944: 1.94, 2.49, 2.58\n\n\n- Jun 1936: 2.58, 3.15 | Jun 1941: 2.01, 2.70 | Jun 1944: 1.91, 2.49, 2.58\n- Jul 1936: 2.58, 3.12 | Jul 1941: 1.98, 2.66 | Jul 1944: 1.89, 2.49, 2.59\n\nThis is extremely problematic since I need 1938 corporate bond yields but they're completely absent from the table. The corporate column specifically starts in 1944, leaving 1938 with no data at all.\n\nLooking at the footnote clarifies why: corporate bonds were calculated as Saturday averages until April 1, 1938, then switched to daily averages afterward. This suggests the yield information might simply be unavailable in the Treasury Bulletin, or perhaps published separately in a different format or source I haven't located yet.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_function_iog2w2heiejb_1","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Looking at table with different grouping to understand structure better  \nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1947_02_page_87.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Parse the monthly table in its raw form  \n# Find the actual data rows with actual numeric values\nlines = content.split('\\n')\n\n# Look for the section containing 1936 data\nin_monthly_section = False\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'Monthly series' in line:\n        in_monthly_section = True\n    if in_monthly_section and '</table>' in line:\n        # Print surrounding context\n        for j in range(max(0, i-5), min(len(lines), i+10)):\n            if lines[j].strip():\n                print(lines[j])\n        break\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
